<.shell title="Switch" current={:switch}>
  <h1>Switch</h1>
  <p class="lead">A setting that changes the moment it's tapped.</p>
  <.used_on pages={["taking attendance at the door", "the ID card check"]} />

  <div class="demo">
    <div class="max-w-100 space-y-4">
      <.switch id="e-sound" label="Sound" checked>A tone for each scan.</.switch>
      <.switch id="e-off" label="Off" />
      <.switch id="e-disabled" label="Disabled" checked disabled />
      <.switch id="e-focus" label="Keyboard focus" class="is-focus" />
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>When to use</h2>
  <p>A setting with no save button, such as Sound on the door's scan page.</p>

  <h2>When not to use</h2>
  <p>
    Inside a form with a save button. Use a <a href={page_path(:checkboxes)}>checkbox</a>: a switch says the change already happened.
  </p>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <p>Label on the leading edge, switch on the trailing edge, a 48 by 28px track.</p>

  <h3>Compact</h3>
  <div class="demo">
    <div class="max-w-100">
      <.button variant={:success} class="w-full">Scan ID cards</.button>
      <.switch id="e-compact" label="Sound" compact checked class="mt-2" />
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="spec">
    One page-level setting under the page's main action, such as Sound under the scan button. A small muted label and the switch, together on the trailing edge. No hint. The track stays full size, since it's tapped in a hurry.
  </p>

  <h2>In the app</h2>
  <p>
    <code>&lt;.switch id="…" label="…"&gt;</code>, with <code>compact</code> for the small one.
  </p>
</.shell>
